Jules: Pushed a PR that consolidates streaming snippets and adds a short section on client-side buffering and rate policies. Preview: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3899 — can folks sanity-check edge cases?

Katerina: Quick scan looks good. Two suggestions: call out default client buffer size and recommend draining before close. Example (Python):```python
for chunk in client.stream_messages(req):
    if chunk.backpressure_hint:
        # slow down producer or flush buffers
        time.sleep(0.1)
    handle(chunk)
```
Add note: default buffer = 64KB, configurable via client.buffer_size.

Omar: TS snippet should show a tiny pause when buffered bytes exceed threshold so readers see a practical pattern:```ts
let buffered = 0;
for await (const part of client.stream.read(req)) {
  buffered += part.size;
  if (buffered > 64 * 1024) await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 50));
  render(part.text);
  buffered -= part.size;
}
```
Also add an explicit one-liner distinguishing streams vs pagination and a small backoff mention for RATE_LIMIT.

Jules: Good calls. I'll add a cross-language pseudocode for exponential backoff (keeps it short) and the one-liner: "streams = incremental deltas; pagination = discrete pages via next_token".

docs-ci: Preview deployed: https://docs-preview.redwood.ai/pr-3899 — build passed :white_check_mark:

Katerina: Found a broken anchor in the migration guide pointing to #stream-old. Pushed a tiny fix to update to #streaming-patterns and added a 1-line redirect note.

